# Laboratory samples, analysis reports, blood bank and tissue products.
ent-NCLabSampleVial = sample vial
ent-NCLabSampleVial.desc = A sealed vial holding a sample taken from a patient. What is inside is only known to a laboratory.
ent-NCLabBloodSampler = blood sampler
ent-NCLabBloodSampler.desc = A syringe that draws a small blood sample into a vial.
ent-NCLabWoundSwabKit = wound swab kit
ent-NCLabWoundSwabKit.desc = Sterile swabs for taking a sample from a wound.
ent-NCBloodBagFilled = donor blood bag
ent-NCBloodBagFilled.desc = A bag of donated whole blood. It must be matched to the recipient and kept cold.
ent-NCBloodBagEmpty = empty blood collection bag
ent-NCBloodBagEmpty.desc = An empty bag for collecting blood from a donor.
ent-NCLabCultureStation = culture station
ent-NCLabCultureStation.desc = Grows cultures from samples to find infections and the antibiotics that work on them, and tests compounds on living tissue.
ent-NCLabMetabolicAnalyzer = metabolic analyzer
ent-NCLabMetabolicAnalyzer.desc = Reads the blood chemistry of a sample: blood group, compounds and how the body is responding to them.
ent-NCLabTissueIncubator = tissue incubator
ent-NCLabTissueIncubator.desc = Grows tissue products from seed cultures. It needs power and a person to load it and to collect the result.
ent-NCLabTissueSeedSkin = synthetic skin seed culture
ent-NCLabTissueSeedSkin.desc = A seed culture that grows into a synthetic skin dressing.
ent-NCSyntheticSkinDressing = synthetic skin dressing
ent-NCSyntheticSkinDressing.desc = A grown dressing used like a sterile bandage.
